Backend
  In your terminal, run:
  cd /Users/jonathanbeltran/service-center/backend
  source venv/bin/activate
  ADMIN_PASSWORD=yourpassword uvicorn main:app --reload
 You should see Uvicorn running on http://127.0.0.1:8000.

Frontend

  Open both files directly in your browser:
  - frontend/index.html — the worker shift picker
  - frontend/admin.html — the admin panel
How scheduling works
  Supervisor panel (admin.html) has three tabs:
  1. Create Schedule: set the period (start and end dates), shift sizes, and
     import workers. This is a draft. It saves as you type, but workers see
     none of it.
     "Autofill Empty Shifts" (on by default): when workers' picks leave
     required seats empty, each one goes to the worker with the fewest shifts
     that week, lowest priority points breaking ties. Forced seats show as
     [JB] on the results and in the Excel export.
  2. Preview Schedule: shows the empty schedule built from the draft. Click a
     cell to mark that shift as incentive pay (green); workers see the same
     green marking when picking shifts and on the posted schedule. Click a
     day's name to give that one day its own shift sizes, yellows and an
     optional note (e.g. a holiday); other days keep the defaults, and the
     note goes in the Excel notes row. Pressing
     "Create Schedule" publishes it. Workers can then open index.html, pick
     their initials, and rank shifts for each week. Coming back later reloads
     what they already submitted. Switching to "Can't work" lets a worker
     mark shifts they absolutely cannot work; autofill never assigns those to
     them. Pressing Create Schedule again re-publishes
     the draft; submissions for weeks no longer in the period are deleted.
     "Remove from Staff View" takes the schedule down so workers see nothing.
     The draft and submitted shifts are kept; Create Schedule posts it again.
  3. Run Schedule: shows who has submitted, runs the algorithm on the published
     schedule, and shows the result. Workers never see it in the app;
     "Download Excel" produces a workbook (one sheet per week, laid out from
     backend/template.xlsx) for the supervisor to share.

Persistence
  All state (draft, published schedule, submissions, results) is saved to a
  JSON file. Default: backend/store.json. Override with DATA_FILE.
  On Railway, attach a volume and set DATA_FILE=/data/store.json so submissions
  survive redeploys and restarts.
